ASSET TYPES, PREVIEW AND LOCAL DISTRIBUTION
Design note — v0.1 — 2026-09-29
Status: PARTLY BUILT — see the divergence table in section 4. The check set,
the download and the library's image thumbnails exist; upload types, preview
for game assets and format compliance do not. Decisions still open are marked
in section 6.

================================================================================
1. WHAT THIS SECTION COVERS
================================================================================

Three related capabilities, raised together but separable:

  A. Upload types — Blender, Nuke, Unreal, Maya, images. Per-type rules,
     validation and handling. Today `asset_type` is free text. FILE CONTENTS ARE
     INSPECTED — `content_matches_extension` reads the first 512 bytes and
     matches them against a format signature table (shared/assetRules.mjs), so a
     JPEG renamed .png is caught. What does NOT exist is FORMAT COMPLIANCE:
     polygon counts, texture dimensions, naming conventions.

  B. Preview — seeing the asset on the website, so an approver can judge it
     without downloading.

  C. Download to the approver's machine — where they have a working copy of
     the game in development, so they can review the asset in situ.

The immediate driver: the approval workflow is now reachable (Phase 1) but
still BLIND. An approver sees an asset name, a version note, a file list with
sizes and hashes — and cannot look at the actual bytes. Reviewing a submission
is currently an act of faith. See TODO item 6.

